<p>Syntax notes:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Extra spaces between <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">|</code>, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">-</code>, <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">:</code>, are ignored and do not affect the layout.</li>
  <li>By default the header row is <strong>centered</strong>, and the content is left-aligned.</li>
  <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">-:</code> means the content and the header are right-aligned.</li>
  <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">:-</code> means the content and the header are left-aligned.</li>
  <li><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">:-:</code> means the content and the header are centered.</li>
  <li>Extra spaces between <strong>content</strong> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">|</code> are ignored.</li>
  <li>The first <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">|</code> and the last <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">|</code> on each line can be omitted.</li>
  <li>There must be at least one <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">-</code>.</li>
</ul>

<p>I always forget how to write a markdown table.</p>

<p>If you need to add a column, you can copy and paste the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">|</code> from the previous row and the <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">|:-----:|</code> from the row below.</p>

